Subject: dlm_maximage 256 KiB; a file over it is ENOLOAD with a line

C3-1 version 4: a module's image is at most 256 KiB and its file is
smaller.  The core's own allocations for a module are KM_SLEEP and grow
with it, and U4 found that a running box gives one request at most
256 KiB; a KM_SLEEP request above that never returns.  lf_hashload's
refusal of a file at the limit was a silent ENOMEM; it is ENOLOAD with
the console line C3-1 section 4 asks for.  The state harness gains pmf,
a small image in a file over 8 KiB.

--- a/dlmconf.c
+++ b/dlmconf.c
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 
 #include "dlm.h"
 
-long	dlm_maximage = 2 * 1024 * 1024;	/* largest image, bytes */
+long	dlm_maximage = 256 * 1024;	/* largest image and file, bytes (C3-1 6) */
 int	dlm_verbose = 0;		/* undefined symbols on the console */
 int	dlm_def_unload_delay = 60;	/* seconds (DEF_UNLOAD_DELAY) */
 int	dlm_unload_wake = 60;		/* seconds (UNLOAD_WAKE) */
--- a/dlm_core.c
+++ b/dlm_core.c
@@ -459,7 +459,8 @@
 		if (n == cap) {
 			if (cap >= dlm_maximage) {
 				dlm_free(b, cap);
-				return ENOMEM;
+				printf("dlm: %s: its file is over the limit\n", lf->lf_mod->m_name);
+				return ENOLOAD;
 			}
 			nb = dlm_zalloc(cap * 2);
 			bcopy(b, nb, n);
